                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239299579",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198207083779",
                            "num_reviews": 1364,
                            "playtime_forever": 248,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 248,
                            "playtime_at_review": 248,
                            "last_played": 1793735750
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Oh what a bizarre game.  I swear there was one event in there that came out of nowhere!\n\nAnyway, as with these type of games you have to read through all the Bad Ends and Good Ends (but are they really good...?) to get to the \"True End\".\n\nI gotta say though...  Anytime you get to the True End...  It's hella rewarding.  Just because you already have everything figured out and you get to see the final, final conclusion.\n\nAs for the rest:\n\n- It has science talk.  A lot of it.  We don't get taught nothin' in school nowadays, so I couldn't comprehend any of it whatsoever.  I DID think it was cool how they created an \"alternative\".  Mhm.\n\n- Romance.  Ah romance...  This is another game where I will say \"why the hell is it in here?\"...  Like the whole time I was reading?  I just wanted to know the conclusion to the mystery, not people getting together.  (Which goes against my whole spirit being 90% submerged in romance).\n\nI am not sure why it was put in...  But it's really nothing major or important.  It just...  Exists.\n\nAh yes and some parts were funny...  And you gotta do a \"pipe puzzle\" to select a choice.  Every.  Single.  Time.  T_T\n\nEh.  Whichever.  This one kept my interest.\n\n(PPS: I have no clue wth was going with that \"one dream\" with the Scientist and Bradley and ah well...  The one kissing scene you get from the Angry one is pretty worth it.  Heh heh.)",
